            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0395" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890g.01/233: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-24T11:00:00+00:00">December 24, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 24—10:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>389. Department’s 352, December 19, 4 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d246-f1"/> I
                    have received an oral message from the Foreign Office stating that Jafar Pasha
                    is agreeable to the note contained in Department’s 317, November 27, 1 p.m. The
                    Foreign Office suggests proceeding with the signatures sometime during the week,
                    beginning January 6, to which I shall agree, failing instructions to the
                    contrary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
